linux-patch-api (2.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix self-update restart race: spawn package-manager processes in own process group
  * Remove kill_on_drop(true) from package-manager spawns to prevent SIGKILL on agent stop
  * Timeout kills now target the process group (negative PID) to clean up subprocesses
  * All distro postinst scripts: immediate systemctl restart instead of 300s delayed timer
  * Add libc as direct dependency for process-group signal handling

 -- Kelly Slavens <kwslavens@gmail.com>  Sun, 20 Jul 2026 20:45:00 +0000

linux-patch-api (2.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Major simplification: remove self-update state machine
  * Self-update is now just: refresh cache, install package, postinst restarts service
  * Remove upgrade-state.json, upgrade-pending marker, fallback timer, drain logic
  * Remove startup recovery mode and version verification
  * Remove repo config self-heal from self-update path (was breaking repo configs)
  * Fix tracking job leak in health check and patch list handlers
  * Fix stale apt/dpkg lock cleanup (#173)

 -- Draco-Lunaris-Echo  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 23:30:00 +0000

linux-patch-api (2.4.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Release v2.4.4
  * fix: add pre-flight stale apt/dpkg lock cleanup (#173)
  * Detects and removes stale lock files from killed apt/dpkg processes
  * Prevents self-upgrade failures caused by stuck apt-get update holding locks

